# Finish every turn

End every turn that did work in two parts, in this order.

1. What changed. A short explanation.
2. Whether the owner has to act.

If the next code cannot exist until the owner acts, the second part is a title and a numbered list. Each step is one plain sentence. A command step includes the command, the directory, and how to tell it worked. Nothing after the list.

If the owner does not have to act, the second part is this sentence and nothing else after it:

```text
You do not need to do anything.
```

That sentence is not a stop. Do not wait for the owner to say continue. Keep building the next work that does not need them.

A store step, a domain, a certificate, or a legal review goes under `Manual steps for the end` in `docs/build-progress.md`. Do not ask for it in that turn. Record a Firebase deploy there too, and still say it in the turn.

Every turn that did work ends with one Firebase line, after the owner section.

If the dev project must be updated for this change to work, that line is a title and a numbered list. Name only what changed: Cloud Functions, Firestore rules, indexes, Storage rules, Hosting, or a published Firestore document such as a form mapping. Each command includes the directory and how to tell it worked. Production is never in that list.

If nothing on Firebase changed, the line is this sentence and nothing else:

```text
Firebase does not need a redeploy.
```

A max-length ask is a real stop. That reply is only the numbered list of field name and suggested max.

```text
Dev rules deploy

1. From the repo root, run the deploy command.
2. Success is a completed deploy.
```
